+++ b/releasenotes/notes/fix-statistics-through-wrapper-3b9f1d6a2c7e4480.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    ``func.statistics`` is now kept up to date when a ``@retry``-decorated
+    function is wrapped by another decorator that uses ``functools.wraps``.
+    Previously the outer wrapper's ``statistics`` stayed as an empty ``{}``.
+    The outer and inner wrappers now share the same ``statistics`` object,
+    for both sync and async functions. Note that ``func.statistics`` is now a
+    live view of the calling thread's statistics rather than a plain
+    ``dict``: it compares equal to a dict and supports the usual mapping
+    operations, but ``isinstance(func.statistics, dict)`` is now ``False``.
